--- A function a part writes into its own record is typed by the
--- program's call through the record's field: lib/tree.co makes its
--- nodes with its own `same` — bare, and in the list that types an empty
--- one — and calls through the field, `n.f[d]`, only in `walked`, which
--- only the program calls. Validated alone, without the program's calls,
--- the part had refused `same` in both modes ("handed as a value, and
--- nothing types its parameters"), though the program typed it and the
--- same lines in one file ran (Lory's gui.co, a control's painter). The
--- program's own `doubled`, handed into the field through the part's
--- parameter, is typed by the same call.
use lib.tree

fn doubled[d]
    d.v = d.v * 2.0
    return d

t = tree.top[[tree.leaf['a'], tree.leaf['b']]]
log[tree.walked[t, 0.0]]
log[tree.walked[tree.top[[tree.leaf['a'], tree.drawn['c', doubled]]], 0.0]]
